content:
Here are the domain objects:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Customer",
      "description": "Person who explores products and buys skateboards"
    },
    {
      "name": "Catalogue",
      "description": "Collection of skateboard models offered to customers",
      "attributes": [
        "Skateboard Model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Skateboard Model",
      "description": "Specific model type listed in the catalog",
      "attributes": [
        "Description"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Description",
      "description": "Text explaining features or usage of a skateboard model"
    },
    {
      "name": "Skateboard",
      "description": "Physical skateboard purchased or delivered",
      "attributes": [
        "Skateboard Model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Review",
      "description": "Customer feedback about a purchased skateboard",
      "attributes": [
        "Skateboard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Sales Associate",
      "description": "Employee helping customers choose and buy skateboards"
    },
    {
      "name": "Purchase",
      "description": "Record of a customer buying a skateboard"
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery",
      "description": "Process of sending a purchased skateboard to a customer"
    },
    {
      "name": "Product Specialist",
      "description": "Expert evaluating models and refining catalog content"
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory Manager",
      "description": "Employee overseeing stock and warehouse data"
    },
    {
      "name": "Stock Levels",
      "description": "Information showing how many skateboards are available",
      "attributes": [
        "Skateboard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Reorder",
      "description": "Action of requesting new stock for low-quantity skateboards"
    },
    {
      "name": "Shipment",
      "description": "Incoming delivery of skateboards or accessories to the warehouse"
    },
    {
      "name": "Warehouse System",
      "description": "System tracking product availability and stock data",
      "attributes": [
        "Stock Levels"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Help me find the associations.  

#### Task:
- Draw connections between objects that have an association. 
- Name each object and add a description that captures the meaning of the association.
- Return the associations in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "associations": [
    {
      "from": "...",
      "to": "...",
      "description": "..."
    }
  ]
}
```

Here are the associations:
```json
{
  "associations": [
    {
      "from": "Customer",
      "to": "Catalogue",
      "description": "Customer looks through the Catalogue"
    },
    {
      "from": "Customer",
      "to": "Purchase",
      "description": "Customer makes a Purchase"
    },
    {
      "from": "Sales Associate",
      "to": "Purchase",
      "description": "Sales Associate helps complete the Purchase"
    },
    {
      "from": "Purchase",
      "to": "Skateboard",
      "description": "Purchase includes a Skateboard"
    },
    {
      "from": "Sales Associate",
      "to": "Delivery",
      "description": "Sales Associate arranges the Delivery"
    },
    {
      "from": "Delivery",
      "to": "Skateboard",
      "description": "Delivery sends the Skateboard"
    },
    {
      "from": "Customer",
      "to": "Delivery",
      "description": "Customer receives the Delivery"
    },
    {
      "from": "Customer",
      "to": "Review",
      "description": "Customer writes a Review"
    },
    {
      "from": "Product Specialist",
      "to": "Catalogue",
      "description": "Product Specialist updates the Catalogue"
    },
    {
      "from": "Product Specialist",
      "to": "Skateboard Model",
      "description": "Product Specialist evaluates the Skateboard Model"
    },
    {
      "from": "Product Specialist",
      "to": "Description",
      "description": "Product Specialist creates the Description"
    },
    {
      "from": "Inventory Manager",
      "to": "Warehouse System",
      "description": "Inventory Manager works with the Warehouse System"
    },
    {
      "from": "Inventory Manager",
      "to": "Stock Levels",
      "description": "Inventory Manager checks the Stock Levels"
    },
    {
      "from": "Inventory Manager",
      "to": "Reorder",
      "description": "Inventory Manager triggers a Reorder"
    },
    {
      "from": "Inventory Manager",
      "to": "Shipment",
      "description": "Inventory Manager handles the Shipment"
    },
    {
      "from": "Shipment",
      "to": "Warehouse System",
      "description": "Shipment updates the Warehouse System"
    }
  ]
}
```
